Goblin Link for Linux handhelds
================================

Copyright 2026 the goblin-link authors.

This directory contains original work plus the third-party assets and
references listed below. None of Meta's / Muse's proprietary fonts, icon sets
or avatar artwork are included or copied.

Ported software — Muse Gadget SDK
---------------------------------
This product includes software ported from the Muse Gadget SDK:

    facebookincubator/muse-gadget-sdk
    Copyright (c) Meta Platforms, Inc. and affiliates.
    Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.
    Upstream commit: 197033c0acd40946a18dc7edc4136f022c08a369

The `muse-proto` crate (crates/muse-proto) is a Rust port of the wire layer
of that SDK, specifically the Python modules:

    noise/noise_xx.py      -> src/noise.rs
    noise/_proto.py        -> src/wire.rs
    noise/envelope.py      -> src/envelope.rs
    noise/framing.py       -> src/framing.rs
    noise/transport.py     -> src/transport.rs
    link_client.py         -> src/control.rs  (encode_message, MessageDecoder)
    ble_framing.py         -> src/ble.rs

The `muse-pair` crate (crates/muse-pair) is a Rust port of the SDK's Bluetooth
pairing, specifically:

    pairing.py              -> src/session.rs
    ble_framing.py          -> src/framing.rs
    ble_setup.py            -> src/setup.rs
    ble_server_dbusnext.py  -> src/ble.rs  (a TrimUI adaptation of ble_server.py)

The `muse-link`, `goblind` and related crates likewise use that SDK as a
protocol reference and test-vector source.

The test vectors under crates/muse-proto/tests/vectors and
crates/muse-pair/tests were generated from that reference (tools/dump_vectors.py
for the former) and contain only synthetic keys and values.

